Homework 2 Synopsis – Tarek Elshahawi

This is a patient registration form for Tarek Medical.
It includes the required blocks and validations from Homework 1, and expands to support more dynamic features.

What the site does:
- Collects name, address, medical history, contact info, and login credentials.
- Displays tooltips on hover using title attributes.
- Prevents bad input with regex patterns.
- Uses JavaScript to validate passwords, date ranges, and slider behavior.
- Redisplays all input via a dynamic Review button before final submission.

What I’m happy with:
- Password logic was successfully implemented using regex, lowercase checks, and a match condition.
- The salary slider updates in real time.
- The date of birth validation calculates today’s date and 120 years back.

What’s unfinished or could be improved:

- I struggled to load the state dropdown from an external source so I left it hardcoded.
- All errors are displayed together under the review section instead of beside each field.
- The review layout is functional but could be more visually polished.

